{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--appositional-numeral-follows-counted-noun","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--appositional"],"statement":{"en":"When counters like -n/-iw or -p(e) are used, the counted noun often precedes the numeral, placing the numeral in apposition.","ja":"助数詞 -n/-iw または -p(e) が用いられる場合、被計数名詞はしばしば数詞の前に置かれ、数詞は名詞と同格となる。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":["with counters -n/-iw or -p(e)"]},"forms":["-n","-iw","-p","-pe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-09","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0109-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--restrictive-postposition-between-noun-and-numeral","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--appositional"],"statement":{"en":"A restrictive postposition may intervene between the counted noun and the appositional numeral.","ja":"被計数名詞と同格の数詞の間には限定後置詞が介入し得る。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0111-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--copula-ne-pronominal-agreement-before-wa","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--number-agreement"],"statement":{"en":"When the copula ne follows a numeral before coordinative wa, it takes the same pronominal subject affix as the predicate of the following clause.","ja":"数詞に後続するコピュラ ne が等位接続詞 wa の前に現れる場合、ne は後続節の述語の主語と同じ人称接辞を取る。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":["followed by wa"]},"forms":["ne","wa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-06","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0111-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--counters-suffixed-with-ne-form-adverbials","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Counters for persons and things suffixed with -ne form adverbial expressions of quantity.","ja":"人や物の助数詞に -ne が接尾辞付加されると、数量の副詞的表現が形成される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0128-06","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0129-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--classifier-n-iw-counts-human-beings","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--person-counting"],"statement":{"en":"The classifier -n/-iw is used with numerals exclusively for counting human beings.","ja":"助数詞 -n/-iw は数詞とともに用いられ、人間を数えるためにのみ使用される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["-n","-iw"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0104-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0105-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--human-counting-forms-used-adnominally","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--person-counting"],"statement":{"en":"Numeral forms used for counting human beings may also occur in adnominal position preceding the noun.","ja":"人間を数えるための数詞形は、名詞の前に置かれて連体修飾的にも用いられ得る。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["-n","-iw"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-08","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0109-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--sinen-ne-forms-idiom-alone","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--person-counting"],"statement":{"en":"The numeral sinen 'one person' followed by the copula ne forms the fixed idiom sinenne meaning 'alone' or 'by oneself'.","ja":"数詞 sinen「1人」にコピュラ ne が後続すると、「1人で」「独力で」を意味する固定的な慣用句 sinenne が形成される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["sinen","sinenne","ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0111-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--numerals-function-as-pure-nouns","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--predicative"],"statement":{"en":"Numerals may stand alone without modifying an overt noun, functioning as pure nouns meaning simply 'one thing' or 'one person'.","ja":"数詞は明示的な名詞を修飾せずに単独で立ち、単に「1つのもの」や「1人の人」を意味する自立名詞として機能し得る。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0111-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--pure-numeral-noun-plus-ne-forms-adverbial","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--predicative"],"statement":{"en":"When a numeral functioning as a pure noun is followed by the copula ne, an adverbial expression is formed.","ja":"自立名詞として機能する数詞にコピュラ ne が後続すると、副詞的表現が形成される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0111-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--counters-suffixed-with-ne-form-adverbials","differs_in":null,"note":"Both describe adverbial formation via the addition of ne to numeral expressions."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--basic-numeral-directly-precedes-noun","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--prenominal"],"statement":{"en":"Most nouns can be counted by placing the basic form of the numeral directly in front of the noun.","ja":"大部分の名詞は、数詞の基本形を名詞の直前に置くことで数えることができる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0106-07","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0107-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--basic-numerals-used-only-adnominally","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--prenominal"],"statement":{"en":"Numerals in their basic form are used exclusively in adnominal position.","ja":"基本形の数詞は連体修飾の位置でのみ用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-05","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0109-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--counter-p-pe-counts-things-animals-humans","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--thing-counting"],"statement":{"en":"The numeral classifier -p/-pe is used for counting inanimates, animals, and human beings alike.","ja":"助数詞 -p/-pe は、事物、動物、人間を数えるために広く用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["-p","-pe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0076-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0104-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0105-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--numbers-with-p-pe-appositional-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--thing-counting"],"statement":{"en":"Numerals formed with -p(e) are never used adnominally and always appear in apposition when referring to an overt noun.","ja":"-p(e) を伴う数詞は決して連体修飾としては用いられず、文脈中の名詞を明示的に指示する場合は常に同格の位置に現れる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["-p","-pe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0111-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--appositional-numeral-follows-counted-noun","differs_in":"scope","note":"Refining the general appositional position of counter numerals to the specific restriction that -p(e) numerals never occur adnominally."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--irregular-forms-for-counting-days","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--word-classifiers"],"statement":{"en":"Days are counted using irregular or suppletive forms, such as sineto 'one day', tutko 'two days', rerko 'three days', and ine rerko 'four days'.","ja":"日数は sineto「1日」、tutko「2日」、rerko「3日」、ine rerko「4日」などの不規則または補充的な形式を用いて数えられる。"},"type":"paradigm-cell","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["sineto","tutko","rerko","ine rerko","asikne rerko"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0106-08","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0107-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--temporal-idioms-include-existential-an","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--word-classifiers"],"statement":{"en":"The temporal idioms sine an pa ta '(then) one year' and sine an to ta '(then) one day' include the existential verb an, whereas an is omitted when counting duration.","ja":"「（ある）年に」を表す sine an pa ta や「（ある）日に」を表す sine an to ta という時を表す慣用句には存在動詞 an が含まれるが、期間を数える際には省かれる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"unstated","conditions":[]},"forms":["sine an pa ta","sine an to ta","sine to","sine pa","an"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-07","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0109-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--numeral-nouns-can-occur-either-alone-or-directly","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--appositional"],"statement":{"en":"Numeral nouns can occur either alone or directly following a lexical noun.","ja":"数名詞は単独で用いられるほか、名詞の後ろに置かれて［名詞＋数名詞］の形で用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["sinep","rep","tup"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0273-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--in-the-author-s-ainu-data-in-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--appositional"],"statement":{"en":"In the author's Ainu data, in the [Noun + Numeral Noun] construction, there are no examples of an intervening modifier between the noun and the numeral noun.","ja":"著者の手持ちデータでは、アイヌ語において名詞と数名詞の間に修飾語が入った例はない。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"actual","conditions":["in the author's corpus/data"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0274-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--in-pre-proto-ainu-numeral-classifiers-if-they","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--classifier-debate"],"statement":{"en":"In Pre-Proto-Ainu, numeral classifiers, if they existed, were a productive and distinct feature of the language.","ja":"前祖アイヌ語において、助数詞（存在したとすれば）は生産的で明確な言語特徴であった。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":["if any existed"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:alonso2022@handbook-epub/l0035-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--nouns-denoting-units-that-combine-with-numeral-adnominals","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--classifier-debate"],"statement":{"en":"Nouns denoting units that combine with numeral adnominals to function as nouns or adverbs are called numeral classifiers (助数詞).","ja":"数連体詞に接続して名詞、または副詞として機能する単位を表す名詞を助数詞と呼ぶ。"},"type":"terminology","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0109-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--ainu-does-not-have-numeral-classifiers-counter-words","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--classifier-debate"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu does not have numeral classifiers (counter words) such as Japanese -sō, -nin, or -mai, and all counting expressions are formed simply as numeral prenominal plus noun.","ja":"アイヌ語には日本語の「艘」「人」「枚」のような助数詞は存在せず、すべて「数連体詞＋名詞」で表される。"},"type":"absence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0458-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-number-of-people-acting-together-can-be","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--number-agreement"],"statement":{"en":"The number of people acting together can be expressed either with numeral noun + verb ne + conjunctive wa, or with numeral noun + translative particle ne + verb.","ja":"人数を示す場合、数名詞＋動詞 ne ＋接続助詞 wa という形でも、数名詞＋転成格 ne ＋動詞という形でも表現できる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ne","wa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0297-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--ordinal-numerals-are-formed-using-otutanu-e-g","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--ordinals"],"statement":{"en":"Ordinal numerals are formed using otutanu (e.g., hoshki 'first', tu-otutanu 'second', re-otutanu 'third', ine-otutanu 'fourth').","ja":"序数には otutanu を用いる（例: hoshki「最初の」、tu-otutanu「二番目の」、re-otutanu「三番目の」、ine-otutanu「四番目の」）。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["otutanu","hoshki","tu-otutanu","re-otutanu","ine-otutanu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0078-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--units-of-counting-such-as-ras-sheet-s","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Units of counting such as ras 'sheet(s)' and 'aynu 'person(s)' are classified as numeral units (num).","ja":"ras「〜枚」や 'aynu「〜人」などは、助数詞（num）に分類される。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"example_only","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ras","'aynu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0007-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--forms-where-a-numeral-is-extended-by-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Forms where a numeral is extended by a counter to form a number are always free forms.","ja":"数詞に助数詞が付加されて数を形成する形式は常に自立形式である。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0038-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-suffix-meaning-person-attached-to-numerals-has","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--person-counting"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix meaning 'person' attached to numerals has the form -n after vowels and -iu after consonants.","ja":"数詞に付いて「人」を意味する語尾は、母音の後では-n、子音の後では-iuとなる。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":[]},"forms":["-n","-iu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0064-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-numeral-series-shinen-tun-ren-inen-ashiknen","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--person-counting"],"statement":{"en":"The numeral series shinen, tun, ren, inen, ashiknen, etc., is used exclusively for counting people.","ja":"shinen, tun, ren, inen, ashiknen などの形式は人にのみ用いる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":["when counting people"]},"forms":["shinen","tun","ren","inen","ashiknen","iwaniu","arwaniu","tupesaniu","shinepesaniu","waniu","hotnen"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0077-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--in-the-rayciska-dialect-of-sakhalin-ainu-counting","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--person-counting"],"statement":{"en":"In the Rayciska dialect of Sakhalin Ainu, counting humans from one to five is formed by prefixing the bare numeral stem to 'aynu (e.g., sine'aynu, tu'aynu, re'aynu, 'iine'aynu, 'asne'aynu).","ja":"樺太アイヌ語ライチシカ方言では、1人から5人までの人数は数詞語幹に 'aynu を後続させて形成される（sine'aynu、tu'aynu、re'aynu、'iine'aynu、'asne'aynu）。"},"type":"paradigm-cell","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":["numbers 1 to 5"]},"forms":["sine'aynu","tu'aynu","re'aynu","'iine'aynu","'asne'aynu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0033-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--a-pronominal-affix-or-a-stative-verb-may","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--prenominal"],"statement":{"en":"A pronominal affix or a stative verb may be inserted between an adnominal numeral and the noun it modifies.","ja":"名詞修飾の数詞とそれが修飾する名詞の間に、代名詞的接辞や状態動詞を挿入することができる。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-numeral-adnominal-sine-one-precedes-a-noun","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--prenominal"],"statement":{"en":"The numeral adnominal 'sine' (one) precedes a noun and does not change its form regardless of what noun follows it.","ja":"sine は「一つの」という意味の「数連体詞」で後ろに名詞が来るが，後ろにどんな名詞が来ても形が変わらない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["sine"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0036-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--numeral-adnominals-precede-the-noun-they-modify","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--prenominal"],"statement":{"en":"Numeral adnominals precede the noun they modify.","ja":"数連体詞は修飾する名詞の前に置かれる。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["sine","tu","re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0274-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--a-quantifier-precedes-the-noun-it-modifies-in","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--prenominal"],"statement":{"en":"A quantifier precedes the noun it modifies in Ainu.","ja":"アイヌ語において数量詞は修飾される名詞に先行する。"},"type":"ordering","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0021-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-adnominal-use-of-the-basic-numeral-morpheme","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--quantifier-syntax"],"statement":{"en":"The adnominal use of the basic numeral morpheme occurs much less frequently than the appositional or nominal use of numbers.","ja":"基本数詞形態素の連体修飾的用法は、数の同格的または名詞的用法に比べてはるかに稀にしか現れない。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"measured","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0038-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--in-texts-nominalized-numerals-are-found-to-quantify","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--quantifier-syntax"],"statement":{"en":"In texts, nominalized numerals are found to quantify only subject or direct object nominals, with no attested instances of oblique nominal quantification.","ja":"テキストの調査では、名詞化された数詞が主語または直接目的語の名詞を数量化する事例のみが確認され、斜格名詞を数量化する事例は見られない。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["in examined texts"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0030-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--ainu-numerals-may-occur-with-two-suffixes-p","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--thing-counting"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu numerals may occur with two suffixes: -p ~ -pe for things (from pe 'thing') and -n ~ -iw for human beings (from aynu 'human being').","ja":"アイヌ語の数詞は、事物を表す接尾辞 -p ~ -pe（pe「もの」に由来）および人間を表す接尾辞 -n ~ -iw（aynu「人間」に由来）の2つの接尾辞を伴って現れ得る。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-p","-pe","-n","-iw"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:alonso2022@handbook-epub/l0034-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-complex-numeral-forms-for-2-and-3","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--thing-counting"],"statement":{"en":"The complex numeral forms for 2 and 3 can furthermore take the suffix -pish, as in tuppish.","ja":"2および3の複合数詞形は、さらに接尾辞 -pish を取ることがある（例：tuppish）。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"possible","conditions":["for numerals 2 and 3"]},"forms":["-pish","tuppish"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0076-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-forms-ending-in-pish-may-have-originally","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--thing-counting"],"statement":{"en":"The forms ending in -pish may have originally been distributive numerals meaning 'by twos' or 'by threes'.","ja":"-pish に終わる形式は、あるいは本来「二つづゝ」「三つづゝ」を意味する配分数詞であったとも思われる。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["-pish"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0077-02","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-numeral-sinep-one-thing-can-also-be","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--thing-counting"],"statement":{"en":"The numeral sinep 'one (thing)' can also be used for human beings.","ja":"数詞 sinep「一つ」は人間に対しても使われる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["sinep"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0370-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-prefix-kes-means-every-as-in-kes","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"The prefix kes- means 'every', as in kes-to 'every day', kes-ukuran 'every evening', and kes-pa 'every year'.","ja":"接頭辞 kes- は「毎〜」を意味し、kes-to「毎日」、kes-ukuran「毎夕」、kes-pa「毎年」などを形成する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kes-","kes-to","kes-ukuran","kes-pa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0177-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--okore-means-all-both-everyone-referring-collectively-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"'okore means 'all, both, everyone' referring collectively to the preceding elements, and can also be analyzed as an adverb.","ja":"'okore は「全部の、〜とも、みんな」と全部まとめていう表現であり、副詞と考えられる場合もある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["'okore"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0110-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--ranke-is-a-postposition-meaning-each-at-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"ranke is a postposition meaning 'each', 'at a time'.","ja":"ranke は「〜ずつ」を意味する後置詞である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ranke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0115-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--most-quantity-nouns-that-do-not-contain-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"Most quantity nouns that do not contain a numeral are always free forms.","ja":"数詞を含まない数量名詞の大部分は常に自立形式である。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0038-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-numeral-iwan-six-can-occasionally-be-used","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"The numeral iwan 'six' can occasionally be used to mean 'many', especially in oral literature and fixed sayings.","ja":"数詞 iwan「6」は、特に口承文芸や固定表現において時に「多くの」という意味で用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":["especially in oral literature and fixed sayings"]},"forms":["iwan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-numerals-tu-and-re-in-combination-can","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"The numerals tu and re in combination can mean 'many', and in this meaning they are often reinforced by the prefix o-.","ja":"数詞 tu と re を組み合わせると「多くの」を意味することができ、この意味では接頭辞 o- によって強められることがしばしばある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["tu","re","o-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--quantity-nouns-like-poronno-a-lot-ponno-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"Quantity nouns like poronno 'a lot', ponno 'a little', opitta 'all', and inne 'a great many people' can occur in apposition to the noun they modify or function as pure nouns.","ja":"poronno（たくさん）、ponno（少し）、opitta（すべて）、inne（大勢の人）などの数量名詞は、修飾する名詞と同格の位置に置かれることも、自立名詞として機能することもできる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["poronno","ponno","opitta","inne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0112-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--among-quantity-nouns-only-poronno-and-ponno-can","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"Among quantity nouns, only poronno and ponno can occur in adnominal position.","ja":"数量名詞のうち、poronno と ponno のみが連体修飾の位置にも現れる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["adnominal position"]},"forms":["poronno","ponno"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0112-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-morpheme-ranke-functions-as-a-restrictive-postposition","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"The morpheme ranke functions as a restrictive postposition after quantity nouns, carrying a distributive meaning '— each'.","ja":"ranke は数量名詞の後で限定後置詞として機能し、「〜ずつ」という配分的な意味を持つ。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["after quantity nouns"]},"forms":["ranke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0171-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--op-tta-and-its-inflected-forms-c-pitta","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--universal-quantifiers"],"statement":{"en":"'opítta and its inflected forms c-ópitta and 'eci-'opítta do not contrast with personal pronouns and do not belong to the personal pronoun paradigm, but share functions with quantity nouns such as sinép 'one' and sinén 'one person'.","ja":"'opítta および人称接辞のついた c-ópitta, 'eci-'opítta は人称代名詞と対立するわけではないため人称代名詞の系列には属さず，sinép や sinén などの数量名詞と共通の職能を持っている。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["'opítta","c-ópitta","'eci-'opítta"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tamura1972@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0020-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--ainu-possesses-two-word-classifiers-used-with-numbers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--word-classifiers"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu possesses two word-classifiers used with numbers: to for counting days and suy for counting times.","ja":"アイヌ語には数詞とともに用いられる2つの語助数詞、すなわち日数を数える to と回数を数える suy がある。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["to","suy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:alonso2022@handbook-epub/l0034-12","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--the-suffix-sui-is-used-to-form-iterative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--word-classifiers"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -sui is used to form iterative numerals (e.g., ar-sui 'once', tu-sui 'twice', re-sui 'three times').","ja":"反復数には -sui を用いる（例: ar-sui「一回」、tu-sui「二回」、re-sui「三回」）。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-sui","ar-sui","tu-sui","re-sui","ine-sui","ashikne-sui","iwan-sui","arwan-sui","tupesan-sui","wan-sui","hempak-sui"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0077-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--special-numeral-forms-have-developed-for-counting-days","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--word-classifiers"],"statement":{"en":"Special numeral forms have developed for counting days: shine-to 'one day', tutko 'two days', rerko 'three days', ine-rerko 'four days', iwan-rerko 'six days', and hempak-rerko 'how many days'.","ja":"日数を数えるには特別な形式が発達している（shine-to「一日」、tutko「二日」、rerko「三日」、ine-rerko「四日」、iwan-rerko「六日」、hempak-rerko「幾日」）。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["shine-to","tutko","rerko","ine-rerko","iwan-rerko","hempak-rerko"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0078-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--when-counting-occasions-or-times-the-special-term","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topics":["topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax","topic:nominal/numeral-classifiers-ordinals-and-quantifier-syntax--word-classifiers"],"statement":{"en":"When counting occasions or times, the special term arsuy is used for 'once', alongside tusuy 'twice' and resuy 'three times'.","ja":"回数（度数）を数える際、「1回」には arsuy という特別な語が用いられ、以後は tusuy「2回」、resuy「3回」などと続く。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["arsuy","suy","tusuy","resuy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-17-39-076Z","status":"grouped"}
